---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About opentier — an open-source, non-commercial directory of developer free tiers."
  canonical="https://opentier.dev/about"
>
  <section class="container-narrow about-page">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Built by one developer, kept honest by being open source.</h1>
    </header>

    <p>
      opentier is run by <a href="https://github.com/Pratiyush" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Pratiyush</a
      >. It started as a personal table of free-tier services I trusted enough to use on real
      projects. The list grew. Friends asked. So it became a public directory with one rule: every
      entry is verified against today's pricing page.
    </p>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>The pledge</h2>
      <ul class="pledge">
        <li><strong>No ads.</strong> Not now, not later, not "just one banner."</li>
        <li>
          <strong>No affiliate links.</strong> Outbound links go straight to the official URL with no
          <code>?ref=</code> parameter.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No paid placement.</strong> Sponsors get a thank-you on the sponsors page. They don't
          get a higher slot in the catalog.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No tracking.</strong> No third-party analytics. No cookies. If we ever add traffic analytics,
          it'll be the kind that runs on the server with zero PII.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>How to help</h2>
      <p>
        Submit services you trust via <a href="/submit">the issue form</a>. Report pricing changes
        as soon as you spot them — the same form covers it. If you want to back the bandwidth bill,
        the <a href="/sponsors">sponsors page</a> has the donate buttons.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>How it's built</h2>
      <p>
        Astro 6 static site. Tailwind CSS v4. Content lives in YAML files validated against a Zod
        schema at build time. Pagefind indexes search at build. Deploys to Cloudflare Pages on every
        merge. Source is on
        <a href="https://github.com/Pratiyush/opentier" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <style>
    .about-page {
      padding-top: var(--space-xl);
      padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    }
    .about-page > p {
      margin-top: var(--space-md);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      color: var(--color-ink-soft);
      max-width: 65ch;
    }
    .eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      color: var(--color-ink-soft);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    }
    .block {
      padding: var(--space-lg) 0;
      border-top: var(--border-rule);
    }
    .block h2 {
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    }
    .pledge {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-sm);
    }
    .pledge li {
      padding-left: 1.5rem;
      position: relative;
    }
    .pledge li::before {
      content: '✓';
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      color: var(--color-coral);
    }
    code {
      background: var(--color-paper-deep);
      padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
      border-radius: 3px;
      font-size: 0.92em;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
